Z||000000||ka4nkf||04-09-2001||09:48 PM||||Thanks very much for your reply. I understand every thing you said, so now I know how they work. My rear E brake does not work. When I pull the E brake handle, the lever on the E brake works. as a matter of fact I can pull it by hand all the way and the brake still does nothing. When I bought the car 6 years ago, I have the invoice where they had just put on new brakes and new rear calipers. The only thing I can think of is they installed the E brake lever with the piston's all the way back and not against the pads. Or they ruined them by pressing them back without removing the E brake lever therefore striping the piston's.I thought if I removed the lever and take a crescent wrench and turn the E brake adjuster, and if I get brakes then that would tell me they put the lever on wrong. But if I don't get any brakes then I know they ruined the piston's. BTW the brakes work great on the car its just the E brake that don't work.I have only put 1000 miles on it since the new brakes and calipers were installed. I think you for your reply'<BR>Don||||reg||1
